roubles that come with keeping a tiny, fragile, easily scarred-for-life hum=
an being alive.

A recent report (https://www.luriechildrens.org/en/blog/millennial-parentin=
g-statistics/?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-8CCe_HbEFhPH0xl9MX4f1gBAhot1gO1jqmtj7FwzmflY=
tUID1afBXeqF9Ni5hbht09uzQTiUKbxkxDaGC9UrYlDEosaw&_hsmi=3D394812731 ) from t=
he Ann & Robert H. Lurie Children=E2=80=99s Hospital of Chicago found:

- 46% feel burned out.

- 58% say they struggle to balance their work and home life

- 85% believe social media creates unrealistic parenting expectations

And while a lot of parents are clearly feeling anxious, it remains to be se=
en whether or not technology is the solution.

It is, however, if you ask OpenAI CEO and new dad Sam Altman, who said (htt=
ps://futurism.com/artificial-intelligence/sam-altman-caring-baby-impossible=
-without-chatgpt?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-8CCe_HbEFhPH0xl9MX4f1gBAhot1gO1jqmtj7Fwzm=
flYtUID1afBXeqF9Ni5hbht09uzQTiUKbxkxDaGC9UrYlDEosaw&_hsmi=3D394812731 ) he =
can=E2=80=99t imagine raising a newborn without ChatGPT.

Special shoutout to Huckleberry (https://apps.apple.com/eg/app/huckleberry-=
baby-child/id1169136078?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-8CCe_HbEFhPH0xl9MX4f1gBAhot1gO1jqm=
tj7FwzmflYtUID1afBXeqF9Ni5hbht09uzQTiUKbxkxDaGC9UrYlDEosaw&_hsmi=3D39481273=
