The elevator pitch: =E2=80=9CDoubles Social is a first-of-its-kind members =
community and app for couple friendships. It connects like-minded couples w=
ith each other, schedules double dates, and plans coveted couples events so=
 you can intentionally expand your social circle and have fun doing it.=E2=
=80=9D

The problem they=E2=80=99re solving: =E2=80=9DThe launch of Doubles Social =
arrives at an important time as societal changes are impacting adult friend=
ships. We're facing a friendship recession as work becomes a dominant socia=
l identity, screen time increases, exurban communities rise, and third plac=
es decrease. Plus, a surge in groups =E2=80=94 from childfree millennials a=
nd sober-curious people to racquet sport enthusiasts =E2=80=94 are actively=
 seeking community.=E2=80=9D

Origin story: =E2=80=9CI got married in June 2024 and have always loved dou=
ble dates. However, once I hit my 30s, I realized that coordinating four di=
fferent schedules to plan a double date was becoming an Olympic sport. Ofte=
ntimes couples say to each other, =E2=80=9CWe should hang out soon!=E2=80=
=9D or =E2=80=9CWe should totally get dinner!=E2=80=9D but then the actual =
planning fizzles out. This conundrum was certainly one I wanted to solve.=
=E2=80=9D

Entrepreneurship advice that=E2=80=99s BS: =E2=80=9CWait until you have rea=
lly high demand for your product before launching an app. The beauty of Dou=
bles Social is the app, and I am happy we started out with the app from the=
 jump.=E2=80=9D

