</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><br><span style=3D"font-weight: bold;">The el=
evator pitch:</span> =E2=80=9CDoubles Social is a first-of-its-kind members=
 community and app for couple friendships. It connects like-minded couples =
with each other, schedules double dates, and plans coveted couples events s=
o you can intentionally expand your social circle and have fun doing it.=E2=
=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><br><span style=3D"font-weight: bold;">The pr=
oblem they=E2=80=99re solving:</span> =E2=80=9DThe launch of Doubles Social=
 arrives at an important time as societal changes are impacting adult frien=
dships. We're facing a friendship recession as work becomes a dominant soci=
al identity, screen time increases, exurban communities rise, and third pla=
ces decrease. Plus, a surge in groups =E2=80=94 from childfree millennials =
and sober-curious people to racquet sport enthusiasts =E2=80=94 are activel=
y seeking community.=E2=80=9D<br><br></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><span style=3D"font-weight: bold;">Origin sto=
ry: </span>=E2=80=9CI got married in June 2024 and have always loved double=
 dates. However, once I hit my 30s, I realized that coordinating four diffe=
rent schedules to plan a double date was becoming an Olympic sport. Oftenti=
mes couples say to each other, =E2=80=9CWe should hang out soon!=E2=80=9D o=
r =E2=80=9CWe should totally get dinner!=E2=80=9D but then the actual plann=
ing fizzles out. This conundrum was certainly one I wanted to solve.=E2=80=
=9D<br><br></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><span style=3D"font-weight: bold;">Entreprene=
urship advice that=E2=80=99s BS: </span>=E2=80=9CWait until you have really=
 high demand for your product before launching an app. The beauty of Double=
s Social is the app, and I am happy we started out with the app from the ju=
mp.=E2=80=9D<br><br></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><span style=3D"font-style: italic;">What are =
